## FRONTEND UX FIXES APPLIED (v1.3.3)

All these bugs are FIXED — do not revert:

1. **Blank screen** (never showed result): `startListening()` returned a Promise that
   hung when `stopListening()` called Voice.stop() but never resolved it.
   Fix: `ListenSession` struct + idempotent `settle()` helper in useSpeech.ts.

2. **TTS Android race**: `Speech.stop()` + `Speech.speak()` same tick — previous
   utterance's `onStopped` called `setIsSpeaking(false)` on new utterance.
   Fix: utterance-ID counter; 50ms Android delay; 3900 char cap; watchdog timer.

3. **WebSocket silent drop**: `sendQuery` returned void, discarded queries when
   socket was closed.
   Fix: `pendingQueryRef` queues one query when disconnected; flushes on ws.onopen;
   `sendQuery` returns boolean.

4. **Processing forever (no escape)**: `startProcessingTimer()` was never called
   from the `handleMicPress` path — no 30s timeout to break out of Processing state.
   Fix: `startProcessingTimer()` called before `sendQuery()` in handleMicPress.

5. **AsyncStorage overwrite**: Loading history from AsyncStorage overwrote live
   in-session messages.
   Fix: functional updater guard: `prev.length === 0 ? parsed.slice(-20) : prev`.

6. **Settings screen showing server URL**: utilsnow.com must not be visible to
   colleagues who share the app.
   Fix: SettingsScreen v1.3.3 shows only Wake Word Active status + About card.
   No server row, no URL, no domain anywhere in the UI.

## WAKE WORD SETUP

Sherpa-ONNX KWS (Apache 2.0) — no account, no key, no expiry.
Model: sherpa-onnx-kws-zipformer-gigaspeech-3.3M (~5 MB int8)
Keywords: `▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35` and `▁HE Y ▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35`
Assets in APK: frontend/android/app/src/main/assets/jarvis_kws/
Runtime copy: expo-file-system.copyAsync(asset:// → documentDirectory/sherpa_kws/)
Audio capture: react-native-audio-record at 16kHz/mono/Int16 → Float32 → KWS.acceptWaveform()

Setup:
1. Install APK from https://utilsnow.com/jarvis/app.apk
2. Open app → Settings → toggle "Wake word" ON
3. Grant microphone permission
4. Say "Hey Jarvis" → app opens Voice screen and starts listening

## MICROSOFT GRAPH INTEGRATION (disabled by default)

To enable live Outlook calendar/inbox:
1. Azure Portal → App registrations → New registration (single tenant)
2. API permissions → Application: Calendars.Read, Mail.Read → Grant admin consent
3. Copy Tenant ID, Client ID, Client Secret into .env
4. Set USE_MOCK_DATA=false
5. docker compose up -d backend

## DEPLOYMENT COMMANDS

```bash
# Rebuild and deploy backend (after any backend code change)
cd /root/jarvis
docker compose up -d --build backend

# Check health
curl https://utilsnow.com/jarvis/health

# Live logs
docker compose logs -f backend

# Rebuild APK (only needed when frontend files change)
cd /root/jarvis/frontend
npx expo prebuild --platform android --clean
cd android && ./gradlew assembleRelease --no-daemon
cp app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk /var/www/jarvis/app.apk

# Git push
cd /root/jarvis && git push origin master
```

## KNOWN ISSUES AND PERMANENT FIXES

1. `attendees` JSON string: asyncpg returns json_agg as string. Fixed in calendar_agent
   with json.loads() parse before iterating.

2. `.env` reload: `docker compose restart` does NOT reload env vars. Always use
   `docker compose up -d backend` (recreates container).

3. Gemini daily quota: 20 RPD on free tier exhausts during testing. Switched to Groq.
   Groq is 1000 RPM with no daily limit.

4. Gemini retry hang: Old Gemini config had max_retries=2, which silently retried for
   hours on quota exhaustion. Now max_retries=0, request_timeout=12.

5. Active nginx config is /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/utilsnow — NOT the project's
   nginx-jarvis.conf. Always edit the active file directly.

6. GitHub PAT lacks `workflow` scope — cannot push .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
   Workaround: commit workflow locally but exclude from push.

7. BootReceiver on Android 14+: Cannot start microphone foreground service from boot.
   Workaround: show notification → user taps → app starts service from foreground.

8. `docker compose restart` vs `docker compose up -d`: restart does not pick up
   .env changes. Use `up -d` (recreates container) after any .env edit.

## TESTING WITHOUT PHONE

Browser test UI: https://utilsnow.com/jarvis/test
Type any query, press Enter or click a quick-query button, see + hear the response.
Uses browser TTS (Web Speech API). 30s local timeout.

## SAMPLE QUERIES AND EXPECTED RESPONSES

Q: "What meetings do I have today?"
A: Spoken natural English summary of today's schedule (or "no meetings today")

Q: "What are my overdue action items?"
A: Lists overdue items with priority and due dates

Q: "Am I free tomorrow afternoon?"
A: Checks calendar for conflicts in that time window

Q: "What did we discuss in the Q4 review?"
A: Semantic search over meeting chunks — returns CFO discussion summary

Q: "Check my inbox"
A: "You have no unread emails" (stub in mock mode; live with Graph API)

Q: "What time is the 1:1 with Bharath?"
A: "Your next 1:1 with Bharath is at 6:30 AM on Tuesday, October 11"

